' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' RELATIONSHIPS
' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

DependencyService ..> UpdateCallbacks : RunUpdate bridge

' DownloaderApp composition (owns these fields)
DownloaderApp *--> UIWidgets       : ui
UIWidgets *--> DownloadControls    : download
UIWidgets *--> PreferenceControls  : prefs
UIWidgets *--> PostProcessControls : postProcess
DownloaderApp *--> UIManager       : uiManager
DownloaderApp *--> PreferenceService : prefSvc
DownloaderApp *--> HistoryService   : historySvc
DownloaderApp *--> LogService     : logSvc
DownloaderApp *--> DependencyService : depSvc
DownloaderApp *--> GPUCapabilityService : gpuSvc
DownloaderApp *--> ReleaseService : releaseSvc
DownloaderApp *--> DownloadStats   : stats
DownloaderApp *--> latestValueThrottle : statusThrottle

' DownloaderApp uses engines (created per session, not stored as fields)
DownloaderApp ..> DownloadEngine   : creates per download
DownloaderApp ..> PPEngine         : creates per post-process

' DownloadEngine value flow
DownloadEngine ..> DownloadRequest : BuildArgs input
DownloadEngine ..> DownloadArgs    : BuildArgs output
DownloadEngine ..> DownloadOptions  : Run / Execute options
DownloadEngine ..> DownloadResult   : Run output
DownloadEngine ..> ProcessCallbacks : Execute bridge
DownloadEngine ..> MediaInfo : Probe returns
MediaInfo *--> PlaylistEntry : entries
DownloadEngine ..> scanResult      : Execute output

' PPEngine internal flow
PPEngine ..> PPCallbacks    : ApplyFilters bridge
PPEngine ..> PostProcessJob : builds & runs
PostProcessJob o--> streamLayout : layout
PPEngine ..> gpuJobGuard    : runJob acquires/releases
PPEngine --> GPUBackend        : GPUBackend field
PPEngine --> BackendCapability : GPUCapabilities field
PPEngine ..> PlanEncoderFn     : buildFFmpegArgsForBackend calls

' GPUCapabilityService internal flow
GPUCapabilityService ..> BackendCapability : Detect / Capability
GPUCapabilityService ..> GPUBackend        : keys its cache by
PlanEncoderFn ..> EncoderPlan  : returns
PlanEncoderFn ..> BackendCapability : reads availability from
GPUBackendOptionsFn ..> GPUBackend : returns labels for
GPUBackendFromLabelFn ..> GPUBackend : parses label to
FormatGPUDiagnosticsFn ..> BackendCapability : formats results from

' PreferenceService
PreferenceService --> FynePreferences : store
PreferenceService ..> AppPreferences  : Load / Save

' HistoryService
HistoryService ..> DownloadHistoryEntry : Load / AppendAll
HistoryService ..> DownloadRecord : AppendAll input

' LogService
LogService ..> SessionConfig : WriteSessionConfig input

' UIManager renders history
UIManager ..> DownloadHistoryEntry : renders

' Theming
darkTheme  ..|> FyneTheme
lightTheme ..|> FyneTheme

' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
' ANNOTATIONS
' ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

note top of DownloadEngine
  BuildArgs() is pure — no I/O.
  Execute() runs the retry loop with
  1 s / 5 s / 30 s back-off.
  Both called from DownloaderApp.runYtDlp().
end note

note top of PPEngine
  ApplyFilters() spawns a worker pool
  bounded to runtime.NumCPU() goroutines.
  Each worker calls runJob() for one file.
  cropdetect runs a silent FFmpeg pass
  before the main encode.
end note

note top of gpuJobGuard
  Owns the GPU-only resource lifecycle
  (gpuSem slot + stall watchdog) so
  runJob() itself stays focused on the
  plain ffmpeg exec/log/rename flow.
  No-op when the job doesn't use GPU.
end note

note top of GPUCapabilityService
  Detect() runs once per app run, started
  in the background via startGPUDetection()
  in helpers.go (called from main() alongside
  checkDependencies()). Caches one
  BackendCapability per GPUBackend applicable
  to runtime.GOOS. PPEngine.GPUCapabilities
  is populated from Detect()'s result before
  ApplyFilters() runs (see postprocess.go).
end note

note top of PlanEncoderFn
  Free function (not a GPUCapabilityService
  method). Always resolves to a runnable
  -c:v arg set: GPU args when the requested/
  auto backend is Available, otherwise the
  existing CPU encoder. WebM always stays on
  libvpx-vp9 regardless of requested backend.
  runJob() falls back to retryWithCPU() if a
  GPU-encoded job still fails at runtime.
end note

note top of PostProcessSettings
  Plain value struct — no Fyne widget
  references. newPostProcessSettings(ui)
  builds it from *UIWidgets. Consumed by
  three free functions in postprocess.go:
  buildPostProcessFilters(s), computeProcessingLoad(s),
  checkPostProcessingEnabled(s).
end note

note top of PreferenceService
  All pref key strings and default
  values live as named constants here.
  AppPreferences is a plain value struct
  — no Fyne widget references.
end note

note top of UIManager
  Owns all secondary window instances
  (About, Help, History, Prefs, PP).
  Enforces singleton: re-focuses
  an open window instead of
  opening a duplicate.
end note

note bottom of ProcessCallbacks
  Callback bridge — lets DownloadEngine
  report progress without importing Fyne.
  Same pattern used by PPCallbacks.
end note

@enduml
